e  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  16 MAY 02 at 12 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan brown lymph node with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fat  The fat is removed and the lymph node is entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch denoting the superior aspect  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm skin ellipse with a 1 0cm nipple and a 3 5cm unremarkable areola area and a 3 5cm unremarkable areolar area  There appear to be two punctate scars at the 10 and 12 0 clock positions located 2 0cm from the nipple  Also remarkable are REMOVED_DATE verrucous lesions measuring REMOVED_DATE and 0 8cm in greatest dimension  located REMOVED_DATE and 6 5cm lateral from the nipple  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a hard ill circumscribed white mass with a gritty cut surface measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and located 0 6cm from the deep posterior margin  appearing to grossly abut the anterior skin surface  located 3 5cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  and a 3 0cm from the medial aspect of the specimen  The remaining parenchyma is composed of unremarkable fibrofatty tissue without nodules  masses or gross calcifications noted  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  B  mass and black inked posterior margin  C  mass with anterior skin taken at nipple  D E  additional sections of mass  F  unremarkable parenchyma at superior aspect of the specimen  G I  blue tinged parenchyma in area adjacent to mass  J  additional sections of mass  K L  lymph node candidates  Resident  CHRISTINE GARCIA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH FOCAL LYMPHATIC PERMEATION BY TUMOR  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SCAR AND CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The sampled resection margin appears free of tumor   RIGHT AXILLARY  LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN MULTIPLE  ABOUT 15  LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Lumpectomy  breast cancer site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm mass with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm that has a 4 1cm healed scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hard  stellate  white mass intermixed with yellow chalky areas  The central portion of the stellate mass contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm dark brown elliptical focus  The mass is 0 4cm from its closest margin  Labeled  Right axillary node  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm mass of adipose tissue with intermixed lymph nodes  Dissection reveals multiple lymph nodes that are entirely submitted  Section Code  A D  representative sections of the mass  E  closest resection margin  F J  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST MASS  RIGHT    report_end  , Negative.
