Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 AUG 96 at 08 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of breast tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm in greatest dimension ill defined nodule  There are multifocal areas of hemorrhage and necrosis on the cut surface  The lesion appears to be at the margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tumor are submitted in cassettes B through E  A section away from the tumor is in cassette F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   IN SITU AND INFILTRATIVE CARCINOMA  THE TUMOR IS GROSSLY AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Arlan F Fuller Jr   M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Grossly_positive.
