ve tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE WITH REACTIVE PARACORTICAL HYPERPLASIA  SCATTERED EPITHELIOID GRANULOMAS  AND PIGMENTED HISTIOCYTES  SEE NOTE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  The lymph nodes in all three specimens show similar findings  which are not specific  Considerations include infection  sarcoidosis  and dermatopathic lymphadenopathy  although the findings are not typical for any of these  A methenamine silver stain for fungi and an acid fast stain are negative  Additional immunohistochemical stains are in progress to exclude an atypical lymphoid infiltrate  and an addendum will follow  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm yellow pink ovoid fibrofatty tissue  with a short stitch designating anterior  and a long stitch designating lateral  and a bowtie designating cephalad  A localization wire is in place  The specimen is inked as follows  cephalad green  inferior yellow  anterior blue  and posterior black  The specimen is sequentially sectioned to reveal a cut surface consisting of approximately 60  yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 40  white dense fibrous tissue  The fibrous tissue displays focally hemorrhagic and cystic areas  The cysts measure up to 0 3cm and are filled with bloody serous fluid  The tract of the localization wire is hemorrhagic and fibrous  A clip is identified within the specimen  No masses are identified within the specimen  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The area of clip is within blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the needle tract within block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary primary sentinel node  54  