chyma is present  Lateral to the biopsy site is rubbery  firm  white to yellow parenchyma with some focal hemorrhage and tiny cysts  0 1cm in average dimension  Nine lymph nodes from the axillary tail are dissected and submitted entirely  SECTION CODE  A D  biopsy site  skin and areolar  E F  closest deep resection margin to biopsy site  G H  lateral parenchyma near axillary tail  I K  representative sections of multiple lymph nodes  Labeled  Lymph node  axillary   is a fibrofatty tissue specimen with a firm  white nodule embedded in the adipose tissue  bisected and submitted entirely in L  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  MRM  PART B  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 24 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast parenchyma  inked and sectioned to reveal yellow to white  firm breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted in entirety in cassettes A through H  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Grossly_close_(multifocal/_broad_front).
