patient s name  unit number  and  left breast    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm mastectomy specimen consisting of a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm skin ellipse overlying yellow to tan white fibrofatty breast tissue  There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect  There is a circular nipple at 12 o clock and a puckered  1 2cm scar at 6 o clock and 2 5cm from the skin margin  The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin inked black The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm firm  tan brown  stellate mass with a biopsy cavity in the center of it  The mass is 5 0cm from the medial margin  5 5cm from the lateral margin  2 8cm from the posterior margin  1 6cm from the anterior margin  and 0 8cm from the overlying skin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm gritty  firm nodule located 4 0cm superior to the main mass  6 5cm from the posterior margin and 4 5cm from the anterior margin  Lastly  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan firm nodule located 1 5cm from the lateral margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and 3 8cm from the anterior margin  The remaining breast tissue is moderately gritty but otherwise unremarkable  No lymph nodes are identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest mass in relation to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest mass in relation to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of largest mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule superior to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule lateral to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved fibrous tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   are 223 grams of yellow to tan white fibrofatty breast tissue and unremarkable tan brown skin measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  There are no palpable masses or visible lesions  Ten representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Gross Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  113  to chromosome 17 signals  160  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MAMMOPLASTY , Negative.
