ISION  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are three containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  E  Ryan  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled with  left mastectomy with Level I dissection   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with attached axillary tail  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan brown skin ellipse present on the anterior surface  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  The skin ellipse contains two unoriented black sutures  There is a 4 0cm curvilinear  well healed scar present approximally between 11 and 1 o clock position  2 5cm from the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm solid cystic tan yellow to tan brown  ill defined mass in the inner and central quadrant approximately between 11 and 1 o clock beneath the overlying linear well healed scar on the skin  The mass lies 0 3cm from overlying skin and 0 5cm from posterior inked margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma shows diffuse fat necrosis  The remaining breast parenchyma contains diffuse nodular fibrous breast parenchyma  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  Two whole lymph nodes are dissected out  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  mass to overlying skin and posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  inner lower quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nodular fibrous