ANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS   2    SENTINEL NODE LEFT AXILLA   REMOVED_CASE_ID    NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Right Axilla  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The sections stained show inadequate numbers of tumor cells for evaluation of staining for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 28 27PM PART A  Lymph Nodes  Right Axilla   Sentinel   REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_CASE_ID    Excision PART B  Lymph Node  Left Axilla  Sentinel  REMOVED_CASE_ID  