  and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm biopsy cavity site that is surface by tan white smooth tissue  Further examination of the biopsy cavity site reveals that it communicates with the exterior surface of the lumpectomy specimen at the extreme lateral margin at a 1 1cm slit like opening  Multiple surgical clips are noted adjacent to the biopsy cavity site  The tissue immediately adjacent to the biopsy cavity site contains slightly firm golden yellow tissue that appears to radiate 0 3cm in all directions from the biopsy cavity site  The remaining breast parenchyma is tan yellow to focally white with no obvious masses or lesions  The biopsy cavity site approaches to within 0 7cm from the medial margin  0 2cm from the superior margin  0 6cm from the posterior margin  1cm from the anterior margin  and 1 3cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Extreme lateral aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity site from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue away from the biopsy cavity site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Extreme medial aspect  Also received in the same container is a 15cm in length by 0 5cm in width unremarkable skin ellipse that is excised to a depth of 0 4cm  Representative section of the skin ellipse is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stewart M Knoepp M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Stewart M Knoepp M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION , Negative.
