 following manner  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Serial sectioning through the specimens reveals areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis lining the biopsy cavity  No tumor is grossly identified  Representative sections of lateral aspect of the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and representative sections of the medial biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm horseshoe shaped portion of tan brown fibroadipose tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating inferior  The inside of the horseshoe is the biopsy cavity and shows focal areas of scarring and shaggy tissue  The biopsy cavity measures 0 8cm from the lateral resection margin  0 4cm from the inferior resection margin  0 5cm from the medial resection margin  and is continuous with the anterior  posterior and superior aspects of the specimen  which is inked with respect to the superior inferior long axis in the following manner  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Serial sectioning reveals a tan yellow fatty cut surface with focal areas of fat necrosis and hemorrhage  Representative sections of the lateral aspect of the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and representative sections of the anteromedial aspect are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY MARGIN   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY MARGIN  EXCISION , Grossly_positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 AUG 95 at 15 15 CLINICAL DATA  Patient status post left mastectomy for an infiltrating ductal carcinoma  Now undergoes a right breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  50   AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  50   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen cannot be evaluated because the specimen was received in two pieces  Infiltrating and in situ carcinoma probably involve both pieces of tissue and probably extend to the margin of both pieces of tissue  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 95 at 16 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 12 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  are two pieces of breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Both have white glistening fibrous parenchyma  entirely submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unknown.
