of right 2nd rib   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft tan pink tissue fragments  The specimen is entirely submitted for Frozen Section as FX  5  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 7 additional containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 16 x 15 x 2cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral portion of the specimen  The anterior surface bears a 5 x 4 5cm tan brown skin ellipse with a 4 x 4cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 2 biopsy cavities  The 1st biopsy site cavity measures 5 x 3cm and is present in the upper outer quadrant approximately between the 9 and 10 o clock positions  This biopsy cavity grossly abuts the anterior margin and is 0 6cm from the closest posterior margin  The second biopsy site cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x 3cm and is present approximately between the 12 and 1 o clock positions  This second biopsy cavity grossly abuts the anterior margin and is 2 5cm from the closest posterior margin  The breast parenchyma in between the two biopsy site cavities contains predominantly tan white rubbery unremarkable fibrous tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma of the specimen is grossly unremarkable and no lesions or masses are seen  No lymph nodes are grossly appreciated within the upper outer quadrant  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first biopsy site cavity  including the closest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second biopsy site cavity  including the closest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma from the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION