Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  BOWES Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Ricard Masia  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Michiya Nishino  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 48 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma and lobular carcinoma in situ diagnosed by core biopsy of the left breast  A 1 7cm mass at 3 o clock was noted on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1    SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  3cm  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma is positive at the superior  medial and lateral margin of the specimen along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Sections of the main lumpectomy specimen reveal an invasive carcinoma with a main tumor mass measuring 1 7cm in maximum diameter  In addition to this main mass  there are many microscopic satellite nodules present suggesting a larger overall mass than the 1 7cm measured grossly  The tumor exhibits two distinct growth patterns  In some areas there is a distinct single file growth pattern characteristic of invasive lobular carcinoma  In other areas  the tumor infiltrates in small angulated nests  typical of tubular carcinoma  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin were performed on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The e cadherin stain is negative in areas of invasive lobular growth pattern and positive in areas of tubular growth pattern  The e cadherin stain is also negative in areas of LCIS and positive in areas of DCIS  The immunohistochemical staining pattern supports the morphologic findings  Thus the overall impression is that of an invasive tubulo lobular carcinoma  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1   BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE MARGIN OF RESECTION  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE   Note  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin is negative in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  Multiple level sections were examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INVASIVE TUBULO LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS 