Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL TISSUE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing guide wire and a stitch designating the deep margin  The deep margin is inked blue  the rest of the specimen is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm firm  white irregular mass abutting one inked black margin and is located within 0 2cm of the closest deep blue margin  A representative section of the tumor in relation to the deep margin is frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  A representative portion of the remaining tumor and margin are submitted in cassettes B E  A representative portion of unremarkable breast parenchyma is submitted in cassette F  Received in formalin  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy  are two pieces of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in greatest dimension  submitted entirely in G K  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL TISSUE   report_end  , Focally_close.
