d in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast 650 grams   is a 650 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen  The surgeon marks the 6 o clock aspect with a stitch  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pale brown skin ellipse on the anterior surface with a grossly unremarkable nipple  The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned from the lateral to the medial aspect  to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm circular tan red breast biopsy cavity with associated firm areas and tan red hemorrhagic clot  This cavity is located in the lower outer quadrant of the breast  2 0cm from the inked posterior margin  3 0cm from the inked anterior margin  1 5cm from the lateral end and more than 6 0cm from the medial end  In addition to the biopsy cavity  scattered throughout the breast parenchyma are multiple intervening tan pinkish white fibrotic areas with scattered blue domed cyst like structures  No other nodules or masses are identified  The specimen is examined for lymph nodes  no potential lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections away from the biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right breast 657 grams  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan pale brown skin ellipse with overlying unremarkable 1 2cm nipple  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm poorly delineated tan pinkish w