Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma with metastases to lymph node  right side                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14 01                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm oriented  irregular shaped  tan white and yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm portion of attached skin  A short surgical stitch designates superior  a long surgical stitch designates lateral  and a blue surgical stitch designates inferior  The specimen is disrupted along the anterior and lateral aspects to reveal a central cavity  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the superior   inferior axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hollow cavity  consistent with a prior biopsy site  The cavity is lined by a tan white  fibrous  disrupted tissue and flanked by numerous  punctate  yellow areas which are grossly consistent with fat necrosis  The biopsy cavity communicates with the posterior and lateral surgical margins  No masses are identified  Cassettes are submitted as follows  A E  Biopsy cavity with closest surgical margins  F J  Additional representative sections of disrupted biop