Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 31 CLINICAL DATA  Previous fine needle aspiration showed adenocarcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBIFORM TYPE WITH NECROSIS AND ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  APPROACHING THE INKED SURFACE IN SEVERAL AREAS  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED SURFACE  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   are two fragments of fibroadipose breast tissue  with the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and the smaller measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  A stitch designates the posterior margin of the largest specimen  A note by the surgeon indicates that the smaller fragment of tissue is additional anterior margin  All specimens are inked black with the posterior surface of the largest specimen inked yellow over black  The additional anterior margin is entirely submitted in cassette A  The largest specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white to white yellow  firm  nodular area  located in the anterior portion of the largest specimen  within REMOVED_DATE to 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The nodule has scattered punctate hemorrhage especially at its periphery  The remaining parenchyma is mostly adipose tissue  and unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B through J  with the nodule in cassettes B through D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Grossly_close_(multifocal/_broad_front).
