Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 07 CLINICAL DATA  Suspicious area on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSIONS  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  60    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma is predominantly tubular and cribriform in pattern  No invasion of vessels is seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40    PRESENT ON FIVE OF SEVEN SLIDES  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors t