Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE FORMING ONE MAIN MASS  REMOVED_DATE CM  IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED FROM THE GLASS SLIDE   AND ONE SEPARATE SMALLER NODULE  0 3 CM  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENDING AWAY FROM AND AT SEPARATE FOCI DISTANT FROM THE MAIN MASS FOCALLY AT THE NEAREST INKED RESECTION MARGIN  NOTE  No blood vascular invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   Both Nodules  The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unremarkable skin ellipse containing the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm white stellate mass  1 0cm anteriorly  there is a second 0 3cm in diameter white retracted nodule with a hemorrhagic core grossly abutting the deep resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is yellow adipose tissue which is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A E  mass with closest margin  J K  sections from 2nd nodule  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with multiple tan pink lymph nodes dissected and ranging in length from REMOVED_DATE to 1 4cm in length  The nodes are submitted in their entirety in cassettes F through I  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Focally_positive.
