Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is no evidence of vascular or lymphatic invasion  The intraductal component is located within the main portion of the lesion  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 19                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm of fibroadipose tissue with a 0 9cm in diameter firm  tan gray irregular area extending to the inked margin  The firm area is submitted in A and B  The remainder is submitted in C and D  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA BUT NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  William H  Yong  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Grossly_positive.
