Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Richard L Kradin  M D  Frozen Section Resident  James E  Davis  M D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Revised Report            Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results Reason for Amendment  1  Corrected Addendum Transcription Error CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  TWO NODULES   SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 4 OF 28 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION AND LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVOLVEMENT  4  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  7  HEALING BIOPSY SITE TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  GRADE  Larger nodule  Grade 2  Smaller nodule  Grade 3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Present  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of larger nodule  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   larger nodule  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   smaller nodule   NOTE  There are two histomorphologically distinct tumor nodules with intervening invasive carcinoma  The larger nodule is composed of predominantly invasive carcinoma  grade 2 of 3  with a papillary architecture and is ER positive  The smaller nodule is located superior and lateral to the larger nodule and is composed of grade 3 of 3 invasive ductal carcinoma with focal spindled morphology and is ER negative  The different morphologies  in combination with the different ER phenotypes  suggest that these tumors represent multicentric disease  rather than multifocal disease  In three of the four positive lymph nodes  the morphology of the tumor cells resembles that of the larger nodule  i e  papillary   The remaining positive lymph node histologically resembles the smaller nodule  The atypical lobular cells are negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  WITH MARKED EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The metastatic tumor cells histologically resemble the tumor cells of the smaller nodule  The tumor cells are identified on both hematoxylin and eosin stain and cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm firm  tan white lymph node with a tan pink  firm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further sections of the lymph node are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right modified axillary radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0 cm specimen consisting of a right mastectomy with attached axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 13 0 cm ellipse of skin attached with an irregularly shaped  REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm areola with a central retracted nipple measuring 1 2cm in diameter  There is bulky lymphadenopathy noted in the axillary tail  The specimen is inked blue anteriorly and black posteriorly  and serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal an area of firm  ill defined nodularity posterior to the areola  This area is comprised of two dominant nodules  The first nodule measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and displays a tan brown to grey to hemorrhagic  granular  firm cut surface with blue discoloration  this nodule comes to within 4 0cm of the posterior margin and abuts the subcutaneous tissue below the areola  The closest anterior margin to this nodule is 3 0cm  The second nodule is lateral and superior to the first and displays a tan grey  granular to shiny  firm cut surface  This nodule measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  and comes to within 2 0cm of the posterior margin and 2 0cm of the anterior margin  Breast parenchyma between the two nodules as well as surrounding the two nodules is tan grey  firm and nodular  The two main nodules are nearly contiguous  No other discrete masses are identified  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  ranging in greatest dimension from 0 5cm to 3 0cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative closest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative closest anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular tissue between two nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast tissue away from two nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisect