Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 34 CLINICAL DATA  Breast cancer diagnosed by fine needle aspiration                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    ALL DESIGNATED MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  One of fourteen lymph nodes is positive for cancer  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY LYMPHADENECTOMY  LEVEL I  LEFT   EXCISION  8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR METASTASIS  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY LYMPHADENECTOMY  LEVEL II LEFT   EXCISION  ADIPOSE TISSUE  NO LYMPH NODE PRESENT  LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY  HOT SPOT  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  LEFT   EXCISION  LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR METASTASIS  LYMPH NODES  AXILLARY HOT SPOT 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LEFT   EXCISION  ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS POSITIVE FOR METASTASIS  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY  HOT SPOT  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LEFT   EXCISION  ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR METASTASIS  LYMPH NODE  RADIOACTIVE  LEVEL 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    EXCISION  ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR METASTASIS  LYMPH NODE  RADIOACTIVE  LEVEL 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    EXCISION  ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR METASTATSIS  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 51     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are eight separate specimens  Labeled  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of breast tissue that is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse  A short stitch designates the superior margin and a long stitch designated the lateral margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a relatively well defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm tan white  hard and gritty mass that is 1 0cm from the superior resection margin  0 5cm from the deep and inferior resection margins  1 5cm from the medial  2 0cm from the lateral  and 1 0cm from the skin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly composed of adipose tissue and breast parenchyma  SECTION CODE  A  tumor in relationship to the superior resection margin  B  tumor in relationship to the deep resection margin  C  tumor in relationship to the inferior resection margin  D  tumor in relationship to the skin  E F  tumor  G  medial resection margin  H  lateral resection margin  Labeled  Left axillary lymphadenectomy  Level I   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of adipose tissue in which are found multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE to 2 4cm  entirely submitted in I through L  Labeled  B  left axillary lymphadenectomy  Level II   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of adipose tissue  entirely submitted in M and N  Labeled  Left axilla  Hot Spot  1  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 3cm piece of tissue  entirely submitted in O  Labeled  Left axilla  Hot Spot  1  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan  rubbery lymph node  submitted entirely in P  Labeled  Left axilla  Hot Spot  1  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan yellow piece of tissue  entirely submitted in Q  Labeled  Radioactive lymph node  Level I  CT 774   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of tissue  entirely submitted in R  Labeled  Radioactive lymph node  Level I  CT 530   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of tissue  entirely submitted in S  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD                                  