cal assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a O 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white  firm  stellate area adjacent to the resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of predominantly of adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  with the stellate area in cassettes A through E  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
