 anterior margin  In addition there is a 3 5cm maximum dimension area of firm non pliable pale white nodular tissue present in the axillary tail  0 2cm from the posterior margin  and 0 8cm from the anterior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm area of yellow and dark brown discoloration in the 12 o clock portion of the breast right underneath the nipple  4 0cm from the closest posterior margin  and continuous possible previous 10 o clock biopsy site  The remainder of the parenchyma appears unremarkable  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior and posterior margins of 10 o clock lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of 10 o clock lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass in axillary region  closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to axillary region  closest anterior margin  blue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of discoloration underneath medial nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected axillary node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible axillary lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Less than 10  of the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain  